  "data": {
    "ruleType": "detachment-rule",
    "group": "Pantheon of Woe",
    "summary": "Your **NECRONS MONSTER** units get this ability:\n\n**Distortion Fields (Aura)**: enemy units up to 6\" from this unit are unravelling. Whenever an attack targets an unravelling unit, the attack gets +1 AP.\n\nAs each phase begins, any of your **NECRONS MONSTER** units can take 3 [mortal wounds](vsdata:core-rule/mortal-wounds) to make the range of its Distortion Fields (Aura) ability 9\" for the rest of the phase.\n\n**Designer's Note**: an army with 2 or more **TRANSCENDENT C’TAN** units has to give each of them [Reletavistic Tether](vsdata:ability/necrons.pantheon-of-woe.reletavistic-tether).\n\n**Necrodermal Binding Abilities**:\n\n- **[Singularity Matrix](vsdata:ability/necrons.pantheon-of-woe.singularity-matrix)** (**C’TAN SHARD OF THE DECEIVER** model, +55 points): this model gets **Lord of Deceit (Aura)**: whenever your opponent uses a [Stratagem](vsdata:core-rule/stratagems) to target one of their units up to 12\" from this model, that use costs 1CP more.\n- **[Quantum Goad](vsdata:ability/necrons.pantheon-of-woe.quantum-goad)** (**C’TAN SHARD OF THE NIGHTBRINGER** model, +45 points): after this model makes an [advance move](vsdata:core-rule/advance-move), it can still declare a charge that turn.\n- **[Animus Damper](vsdata:ability/necrons.pantheon-of-woe.animus-damper)** (**C’TAN SHARD OF THE VOID DRAGON** model, +35 points): once per turn, as [your opponent's Shooting phase](vsdata:core-rule/shooting-phase) begins, pick an enemy **VEHICLE** unit that is [visible](vsdata:core-rule/visibility) to this model. That unit takes a [Leadership test](vsdata:core-rule/leadership-rolls). Attacks by that unit's models get -1 to [Hit](vsdata:core-rule/hit-rolls), and also -1 to [Wound](vsdata:core-rule/wound-rolls) if it failed the test, for the rest of the phase.\n- **[Reletavistic Tether](vsdata:ability/necrons.pantheon-of-woe.reletavistic-tether)** (**TRANSCENDENT C’TAN** model, +40 points): in your turn, whenever this unit uses its [Transdimensional Displacement](vsdata:ability/necrons.transcendent-ctan.transdimensional-displacement) ability to make an [ingress move](vsdata:core-rule/ingress-move) or advance move, it only has to end that move over 6\" horizontally from every enemy unit, not over 8\". If it ends that move up to 8\" from an enemy unit, it cannot declare a charge for the rest of the turn.",
